{#- Art from this campaign's own library that the moment could use, ranked by
    store/context/art.py. Selection happens in code -- which pictures are even
    candidates (the on-stage cast, the current setting, activated and recalled
    entities, the campaign library) and which of those clear the floor. This
    template only lists what it is handed.

    Renders NOTHING when the catalogue is empty, which is every turn on a store
    where nobody has described an image. That is what keeps an install that
    never uses this feature at a byte-identical prompt.

    The handle, not a URL: the model writes the handle back and
    art.resolve_handles rewrites it into markdown before the reply is split
    into posts, so a URL never has to survive being retyped and a handle is
    never stored. A handle naming anything not listed here resolves to nothing
    and is deleted, so there is no failure mode worth warning the model about.

    The handles are printed BARE, not in backticks. They used to be fenced for
    legibility, right under an instruction to write one "exactly as spelled
    below" -- so a model that obliged produced `` `![alt](url)` ``, a code span
    that renders as literal text and never shows the picture. `resolve_handles`
    tolerates a copied pair anyway, but not offering the shape is the half of
    that fix which costs nothing.

    Vars: available_art ([{handle, description}]). -#}
{%- if available_art %}# Available art

These pictures already exist in this campaign. If one of them genuinely fits a
beat in your reply, you may include it by writing its handle on a line of its
own, exactly as spelled below.

{% for art in available_art %}- {{ art.handle }} — {{ art.description }}
{% endfor %}
At most one picture per reply, and only when it earns its place. Most replies
should include none. A picture never replaces describing something in prose:
write the scene as you always would, and add the handle only if the image
shows what you have just written. Never invent a handle that is not on this
list, and never describe a picture that is not on it as though it existed.{% endif -%}
